```http
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Create a user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Faida",
  "username": "faida@example.com",
  "password": "example123"
}

### 2. List all users and their blogs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

### 3. Get one user by ID, including their blogs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1

### 4. Update a user's name using their email username
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/faida%40example.com
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Faida Kulimushi"
}

### 5. Test invalid email (should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "username": "not-an-email",
  "password": "example123"
}

### 6. Test duplicate email (should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Another User",
  "username": "faida@example.com",
  "password": "example456"
}

### 7. Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "faida@example.com",
  "password": "example123"
}

### 8. Create a blog as a logged-in user
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/blogs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Learning Full Stack Open",
  "author": "Faida",
  "url": "https://fullstackopen.com/",
  "likes": 0
}

### 9. List all blogs with their users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/blogs

### 10. Get one blog by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/blogs/1
```